# GitLab Pages custom response headers.
# Cloudflare additionally caches via a Cache Rule (*.json.gz). These headers are the origin backup
# and drive the edge TTL when Cloudflare is set to "Respect origin".
#
# The feed is regenerated daily, so stale-while-revalidate must stay well below that interval:
# at 86400 the edge could hand a consumer day-old CVE data long after a new deploy. The
# verify-published CI job purges the edge outright when CF_ZONE_ID/CF_API_TOKEN are set; this
# TTL is the fallback for when they are not.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=3600

# Keep the datafeed files out of search engine indexes (the .json.gz are not HTML,
# so the index.html <meta robots> does not apply to them).
/*.json.gz
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
